        {
          "name": "get_schema",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:a3a41e77ef876e9abb40c3a8b8fcb2d7eca27c1fafa59d8436a69775771d88cd",
          "description": "Get the JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) for one kind's documents: every field it accepts, with types, limits and descriptions, plus only the shared `$defs` it refers to. `kind` is one value from `list_kinds`, e.g. `sequence`. Use it when `get_example` does not show a field you need. Local and deterministic: 3 to 13 KB per kind, cut from the ~150 KB published schema. Referential rules (unique ids, edges that land on real nodes) are beyond JSON Schema — `validate_document` checks those.",
